---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import ObfuscatedEmail from "../components/ObfuscatedEmail.astro";

const updated = "August 27, 2026";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Sardrobe"
  description="The terms that govern your use of Sardrobe, your private digital wardrobe."
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated={updated}
>
  <section class="legal__section">
    <p>
      These terms form an agreement between you and Omar Kawach, the United
      States-based operator of Sardrobe ("Sardrobe," "we," "us," or "our"). They
      govern your use of sardrobe.com and the Sardrobe app. By creating an
      account or using the service, you agree to them. If you don't agree,
      please don't use Sardrobe.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      Sardrobe is a private digital wardrobe that lets you upload photos of your
      clothes, organize them, create outfits, and prepare packing plans.
      Background removal is performed in your browser before a finished cutout
      is saved. The optional AI feature downloads an open model and runs
      it in your browser without a hosted AI fallback. We may add, change, limit,
      or remove features over time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>AI suggestions</h2>
    <p>
      AI suggestions are generated automatically on your device and may
      be incomplete, inaccurate, or unsuitable. Sardrobe presents them as drafts:
      you are responsible for reviewing selected wardrobe pieces, outfit combinations,
      dates, and packing recommendations before saving or relying on them. On-device planning AI
      is not used to identify or describe individual wardrobe items. Device
      and browser support varies, and the feature may be unavailable or fail to run
      on some devices.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Eligibility and your account</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You sign in with Google and are responsible for your account.</li>
      <li>You must be at least 13 years old to use Sardrobe.</li>
      <li>
        If you have not reached the age of legal majority where you live, you
        may use Sardrobe only with permission from a parent or legal guardian.
      </li>
      <li>
        Keep your sign-in secure. You're responsible for activity that happens
        under your account and must tell us promptly if you believe it has been
        compromised.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      The photos and information you add to Sardrobe are yours. You keep all
      rights to your content. You grant us only the limited permission needed to
      host, store, reproduce, process, transmit, and display it to operate,
      secure, and support the service. This permission is worldwide,
      non-exclusive, and royalty-free, and it ends when the content is deleted
      except for limited provider backups, security records, or legal
      obligations described in the Privacy Policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      You're responsible for what you upload, and you confirm you have the right
      to upload it and allow us to process it as described above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>WebMCP site tools</h2>
    <p>
      On the signed-in app page, Sardrobe registers WebMCP site tools with
      compatible browsers. A browser agent may use them to read wardrobe data,
      images, import drafts, outfits, and packing plans, or to create, edit,
      submit, discard, and permanently delete content through your authenticated
      browser session. Sardrobe does not run a separate agent relay.
    </p>
    <p>
      Agent calls use the same authentication, ownership checks, validation,
      rate limits, and other safeguards as actions taken through the interface.
      Some destructive operations require a <code>confirm: true</code> tool parameter.
      That parameter is a technical safeguard, not a promise that your agent will
      display a confirmation prompt; your chosen agent client controls its
      approval experience.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for the browsers, agents, model providers, permissions,
      and instructions you choose. Actions they take through your
      account are treated as actions authorized by you. Review their privacy and
      security terms and grant only the access you intend. Sardrobe does not control
      data after you direct it to a third-party agent or model provider.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>When using Sardrobe, you agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Break the law or infringe anyone's rights.</li>
      <li>Upload malicious, harmful, or illegal content.</li>
      <li>
        Attempt to disrupt, reverse engineer, or gain unauthorized access to the
        hosted service or other users' data, except to the extent a restriction
        on reverse engineering is prohibited by law.
      </li>
      <li>Misuse the service in a way that harms Sardrobe or other people.</li>
      <li>
        Use automated tools in a way that exceeds documented limits, bypasses
        safeguards, or unreasonably burdens the service.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>
    <p>
      Sardrobe relies on services such as Google, Cloudflare, and Sentry. Their
      services may be governed by their own
      terms and privacy policies. External links, including Buy Me a Coffee,
      take you to services we do not control. Sardrobe is not responsible for
      third-party services, content, availability, or data practices.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Sardrobe materials</h2>
    <p>
      Other than your content and third-party materials, the service's branding,
      design, text, software, and other materials are protected by intellectual
      property laws and are owned by Sardrobe's operator or licensors. These
      terms give you a limited, personal, non-exclusive, revocable right to use
      the service as intended. Open-source components remain governed by their
      stated licenses.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Deletion and termination</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using Sardrobe at any time. You can also permanently delete
      your account from the account menu. After a successful request, your
      active account, wardrobe items, outfits, packing plans, and stored cutouts
      are removed and cannot be restored through Sardrobe. Limited recovery
      copies and security, authentication, or diagnostic records may remain for
      the periods described in the Privacy Policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may suspend or terminate access if you violate these terms, create
      security or legal risk, or misuse the service. Where practical, we will
      give notice, but we may act immediately when reasonably necessary to
      protect the service or others. Sections that by their nature should
      survive termination will remain effective.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Availability and warranties</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep Sardrobe running, but we can't guarantee it will always be
      available, uninterrupted, secure, or error-free. To the fullest extent
      permitted by law, the service is provided "as is" and "as available,"
      without express or implied warranties, including warranties of
      merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, and
      non-infringement. Please keep your own copies of photos or information
      that matter to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Sardrobe is not liable for any
      indirect, incidental, special, exemplary, punitive, or consequential
      damages, or for lost data, profits, goodwill, or opportunities, arising
      from the service. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain exclusions or
      limits, so parts of this section may not apply to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Indemnity</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, you agree to defend and indemnify
      Sardrobe's operator from third-party claims, losses, and reasonable costs
      arising from your unlawful content, your misuse of the service, or your
      material violation of these terms. This does not require you to indemnify
      us for our own unlawful conduct.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms from time to time. When we do, we'll revise the
      "Last updated" date above. If a change is material, we will provide
      additional notice where appropriate. Continuing to use Sardrobe after the
      updated terms take effect means you accept them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>General terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms and the Privacy Policy are the entire agreement between you
      and Sardrobe concerning the service. If any provision is unenforceable,
      the remaining provisions remain effective. A failure to enforce a
      provision is not a waiver. You may not transfer these terms without our
      consent; we may transfer them as part of a reorganization, financing,
      merger, acquisition, or sale of the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the U.S. state in which Sardrobe's
      operator is principally located, without regard to conflict-of-law rules,
      except where the mandatory law of your location provides otherwise.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal__section">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? Email us at
      <ObfuscatedEmail user="omarkawach" domain="outlook" tld="com" />.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="legal__note">
    We've kept this in plain language so it's easy to follow. If anything is
    unclear or you'd like to know more about how your data is handled, just
    reach out. We're happy to help.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
